s, $90 per bottle. This brand’s mission is to be the highest quality producer of Sparkling Wines in Oregon.","section":"Business","block":51,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001199835-26-000061","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000838875","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/838875/000119983526000061/wvvi-10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/7f823f9c9dfa245053d0fe7185c47b302ac30b12eff4274cbbac7b8dabe80092.bin","sha256":"7f823f9c9dfa245053d0fe7185c47b302ac30b12eff4274cbbac7b8dabe80092"}},{"id":"d5e2921344b6e79e16a4706a681cea58079f9ffb9fc4bbd5da8ea8ad4dcb2433","quote":"Under its Griffin Creek label, the Company produces and sells the following types of wine in 750 ml bottles: Syrah, the brand’s flagship, $65 per bottle; Merlot, $65 per bottle; Cabernet Sauvignon, $65 per bottle; Grenache, $80 per bottle; Cabernet Franc, $65 per bottle; Tempranillo, $65 per bottle; Malbec, $60 per bottle; The Griffin (a Bordeaux style blend), $75 per bottle; and Viognier, $45 per bottle. This brand’s mission is to be the highest quality producer of Bordeaux and Rhone varietals in Southern Oregon.","context":"4","section":"Business","block":53,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001199835-26-000061","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000838875","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/838875/000119983526000061/wvvi-10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/7f823f9c9dfa245053d0fe7185c47b302ac30b12eff4274cbbac7b8dabe80092.bin","sha256":"7f823f9c9dfa245053d0fe7185c47b302ac30b12eff4274cbbac7b8dabe80092"}},{"id":"865d51b02ee6c2555697269e62e984427da9b24e8e33d4a3c54621aadf061d45","quote":"Under its Elton label, the Company produces and sells the following types of wine in 750 ml bottles: Pinot Noir, $80 per bottle; and Chardonnay, $80 per bottle.","context":"Under its Griffin Creek label, the Company produces and sells the following types of wine in 750 ml bottles: Syrah, the brand’s flagship, $65 per bottle; Merlot, $65 per bottle; Cabernet Sauvignon, $65 per bottle; Grenache, $80 per bottle; Cabernet Franc, $65 per bottle; Tempranillo, $65 per bottle; Malbec, $60 per bottle; The Griffin (a Bordeaux style blend), $75 per bottle; and Viognier, $45 per bottle. This brand’s mission is to be the highest quality producer of Bordeaux and Rhone varietals in Southern Oregon.","section":"Business","block":54,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001199835-26-000061","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000838875","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/838875/000119983526000061/wvvi-10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/7f823f9c9dfa245053d0fe7185c47b302ac30b12eff4274cbbac7b8dabe80092.bin","sha256":"7f823f9c9dfa245053d0fe7185c47b302ac30b12eff4274cbbac7b8dabe80092"}},{"id":"851c935dcc8145eed523bf04d1237e25d5cdca21ba57841d08db06aaf209c6e4","quote":"Under its Pambrun label, the Company produces and sells the following types of wine in 750 ml bottles: Chrysologue, $90 per bottle; Merlot, $80 per bottle; Cabernet Sauvignon, $90 per bottle; and Malbec, $75 per bottle.","context":"Under its Elton label, the Company produces and sells the following types of wine in 750 ml bottles: Pinot Noir, $80 per bottle; and Chardonnay, $80 per bottle.","section":"Business","block":55,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001199835-26-000061","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-03-24","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0000838875","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/838875/000119983526000061/wvvi-10k.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/7f823f9c9dfa245053d0fe7185c47b302ac30b12eff4274cbbac7b8dabe80092.bin","sha256":"7f823f